Consider the following C program. Assume function parameters are evaluated from right to left:

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int g(int p) {
    printf("%d", p);
    return p;
}

int h(int q) {
    printf("%d", q);
    return q;
}

void f(int x, int y) {
    g(x);
    h(y);
}

int main() {
    f(g(10), h(20));
}
```

Which option is the correct output?

Consider the following C function definition:

```c
int fX(char *a) {
    char *b = a;
    while (*b) {
        b++;
    }
    return b - a;
}
```

Which of the following statements is/are true?

options.B:
Assuming a character array c is declared in main, the call below always returns a value:

```c
char c[] = "abcd";
fX(c);
```

options.D:
Assuming a character pointer c is declared in main, the call below always returns a value:

```c
char *c = "abcd";
fX(c);
```

